    "rationale": "Fix over round 1: the column-block loop now runs n = 0..N//16-1 (5 iterations), so every C column block 16*n is written; the prior M//16 bound covered only n=0, leaving cells unwritten. A's two 16x16 tiles (offsets 0 and 16, stride 32) are loaded once into scratchpad rows 0 and 16, reused across all 5 column blocks \u2014 minimal A traffic of 512 bytes. Per block, the two B tiles (k=0 at offset 16*n, k=16 at offset 80+16*n, stride 80) stream into spad rows 32 and 48, fitting the 80-row scratchpad. Each block: preload B(k=0) with overwrite out_addr (bit31|bit29 = 2684354560, acc row 0), compute with A tile 0; preload B(k=16) with accumulate out_addr (bit31|bit30|bit29 = 3758096384), compute with A tile at spad 16; then mvout the 16x16 accumulator to C element offset 16*n with store stride 320 (80 int32). Computes use accumulated=false (B from the pending preload, bd=GARBAGE_ADDR), giving in-order k=0 then k=16 reduction. Total mvin bytes: 2*256 (A) + 10*256 (B) = 3072, minimal since all 2 A tiles and 10 distinct B tiles are loaded exactly once. Expanded commands: 6 setup + 7*5 loop + fence = 42."
